  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Paved area = courtyard area − fountain area: \\(2x(x + 3) - x^{2} = 91\\).",
    "Simplify: \\(x^{2} + 6x = 91\\). Complete the square: \\((x + 3)^{2} = 100\\), so \\(x + 3 = \\pm 10\\).",
    "Since \\(x\\) is a length, \\(x + 3 = 10\\) and \\(x = 7\\). (Check: \\(14 \\cdot 10 - 49 = 91\\).)"
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Incorrect. This is the value of \\(x + 3\\) from \\((x + 3)^{2} = 100\\); the last step of subtracting \\(3\\) was skipped.",
    "B": "Incorrect. This is the size of the rejected root \\(x = -13\\) with its sign dropped; a length cannot come from the negative root.",
    "C": "Incorrect. This is the result of setting \\(x^{2} = 91\\), treating the paved area as if it were the area of the fountain.",
    "D": "Correct. \\(2x(x + 3) - x^{2} = x^{2} + 6x = 91\\) gives \\((x + 3)^{2} = 100\\), so \\(x = 7\\)."
  },
